IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ip-nouns`
IMPORT `ip-framework`
IMPORT `ip-restraints`

-- Antitrust Guidelines for the Licensing of Intellectual Property (2017), section 4.3:
-- the antitrust "safety zone".
--
-- AGENCY ENFORCEMENT POLICY, NOT LAW. Inside the zone the agencies say they will not
-- challenge the restraint "absent extraordinary circumstances", which the text does not
-- define; the qualifier is kept in the result's name, not taken as an input (fork F9).
-- Outside the zone is not a finding of anything: "licensing arrangements are not
-- anticompetitive merely because they do not fall within the scope of the safety zone",
-- and "it is likely that the great majority of licenses falling outside the safety zone
-- are lawful and procompetitive" (4.3 [pdf page 27]). Whether a restraint is in the zone
-- is "based on the factual circumstances prevailing at the time of the conduct at issue"
-- (4.3 [pdf pages 27-28], n.62): the inputs are the facts at that time.
--
-- No numbered Example applies 4.3 with figures (Example 3 has only "Cf. section 4.3"), so
-- the tests of this module come from its thresholds and conditions.

§ `4.3 Antitrust "safety zone"`

§§ `4.3 condition (1): not facially anticompetitive`

-- n.59 [pdf page 26]: "'Facially anticompetitive' refers to restraints that normally
-- warrant per se treatment, as well as other restraints of a kind that would always or
-- almost always tend to reduce output or increase prices. See section 3.4." Read by the
-- type of restraint, whatever its integration (fork F4).
@ref 4.3, n.59 [pdf page 26]; 3.4 [pdf pages 19-20]
GIVEN r IS A `Restraint in a licensing arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `4.3: the restraint is facially anticompetitive` IF
       `the type of restraint has been accorded per se treatment` (r's `the type of restraint`)
    OR r's `the restraint is of a kind that would always or almost always tend to reduce output or increase prices`

§§ `4.3 condition (2): the markets`

-- 4.3 [pdf page 26]: "the licensor and its licensees collectively account for no more than
-- twenty percent". The sum of each party's own share (fork F1). A share below 0 or above
-- 100, or a sum above 100, is impossible (NOTHING).
@ref 4.3 [pdf page 26]
GIVEN s IS A `Market shares of the licensor and its licensees`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`4.3: the share the licensor and its licensees collectively account for` MEANS
    IF     all (GIVEN x YIELD x AT LEAST 0 AND x AT MOST 100) shares
       AND sum shares AT MOST 100
    THEN JUST (sum shares)
    ELSE NOTHING
  WHERE
    shares MEANS s's `the licensor's share` FOLLOWED BY s's `the licensees' shares`

-- 4.3 [pdf pages 26-27]: "four or more independently controlled technologies in addition
-- to the technologies controlled by the parties to the licensing arrangement that may be
-- substitutable for the licensed technology at a comparable cost to the user", counted
-- once per independent controller (fork F3).
@ref 4.3 [pdf pages 26-27]
GIVEN ts IS A LIST OF `Other technology`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of independently controlled technologies in addition to those of the parties that may be substitutable at a comparable cost` MEANS
    count (nub (map (GIVEN t YIELD t's `who ultimately controls it`) (filter (GIVEN t YIELD (NOT t's `it is controlled by a party to the licensing arrangement`) AND t's `it may be substitutable for the licensed technology at a comparable cost to the user`) ts)))

-- 4.3 [pdf pages 26-27]: the criterion each relevant market significantly affected must
-- meet (each must meet its own: fork F2).
--   * Share data available and accurate: no more than twenty percent, in any kind of
--     market (fork F6 for technology and research and development markets).
--   * No such data, a technology market: four or more independently controlled
--     substitutable technologies besides the parties'.
--   * No such data, a research and development market: four or more independently
--     controlled entities besides the parties with the required specialized assets or
--     characteristics and the incentive (4.3 [pdf page 27]).
--   * No such data, a goods market: the text names no substitute criterion (NOTHING;
--     fork F7).
-- Exactly twenty percent is inside; exactly four is enough.
@ref 4.3 [pdf pages 26-27]
GIVEN m IS A `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`4.3: the market meets its criterion` MEANS
    CONSIDER m's `the parties' shares`
    WHEN JUST s THEN
        CONSIDER `4.3: the share the licensor and its licensees collectively account for` s
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST total THEN JUST (total AT MOST 20)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER m's `the kind of market`
        WHEN `a goods market` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `a technology market` THEN JUST (`the number of independently controlled technologies in addition to those of the parties that may be substitutable at a comparable cost` (m's `the other technologies`) AT LEAST 4)
        WHEN `a research and development market` THEN JUST (`the number of independently controlled entities in addition to the parties that possess the required assets and the incentive` (m's `the other entities`) AT LEAST 4)

-- 4.3 [pdf page 26]: "Whether a restraint falls within the safety zone will be determined
-- by reference only to goods markets unless the analysis of goods markets alone would
-- inadequately address the effects of the licensing arrangement on competition among
-- technologies or in research and development." When it would, every listed market is
-- considered, goods markets included.
@ref 4.3 [pdf page 26]
GIVEN a IS A `Licensing arrangement before the safety zone (4.3)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
`4.3: the markets by reference to which the safety zone is determined` MEANS
    IF a's `the analysis of goods markets alone would inadequately address the effects of the arrangement on competition among technologies or in research and development`
    THEN a's `the relevant markets significantly affected by the restraint`
    ELSE filter (GIVEN m YIELD m's `the kind of market` EQUALS `a goods market`) (a's `the relevant markets significantly affected by the restraint`)

§§ `4.3 The result`

DECLARE `Why the safety zone does not apply (4.3)` IS ONE OF
    `the restraint is not in a licensing arrangement`
    `the restraint is unrelated to the use of the licensed intellectual property`
    `the agencies apply a merger analysis to the transfer`

DECLARE `Why the restraint is outside the safety zone (4.3)` IS ONE OF
    `the restraint is facially anticompetitive`
    `a relevant market significantly affected by the restraint does not meet its criterion`
        HAS `the markets that do not` IS A LIST OF STRING

DECLARE `Safety zone result (4.3)` IS ONE OF
    `inside the safety zone: absent extraordinary circumstances, the agencies will not challenge the restraint`
    `outside the safety zone: the agencies will analyze the arrangement on the considerations of parts 3 to 5, and it is not anticompetitive merely for being outside`
        HAS `why it is outside` IS A `Why the restraint is outside the safety zone (4.3)`
    `the safety zone does not apply`
        HAS `why it does not apply` IS A `Why the safety zone does not apply (4.3)`

-- 4.3 [pdf pages 26-27]: "Absent extraordinary circumstances, the Agencies will not
-- challenge a restraint in an intellectual property licensing arrangement if (1) the
-- restraint is not facially anticompetitive and (2) the licensor and its licensees
-- collectively account for no more than twenty percent of each relevant market
-- significantly affected by the restraint. This 'safety zone' does not apply to those
-- transfers of intellectual property rights to which a merger analysis is applied."
-- n.58: nor "to restraints that are not in a licensing arrangement, or to restraints that
-- are in a licensing arrangement but are unrelated to the use of the licensed
-- intellectual property". n.86: nor to the transfers of 5.7.
-- The order of the checks: what the guidelines cover (1.0: a trademark is not covered,
-- NOTHING); n.58; the merger analysis (when 5.7 says only that the agencies MAY apply one,
-- n.85, whether the zone applies is not settled: NOTHING, fork F8); condition (1); then
-- condition (2) over the markets considered, where one market that does not meet its
-- criterion puts the restraint outside even when another market cannot be decided, and a
-- market that cannot be decided otherwise leaves the answer undecided (NOTHING). No
-- market to consider is a case the text does not contemplate (NOTHING; fork F10).
@ref 4.3, n.58, n.59 [pdf page 26]; 4.3 [pdf page 27]; 5.7, n.85, n.86 [pdf page 36]
GIVEN a IS A `Licensing arrangement before the safety zone (4.3)`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Safety zone result (4.3)`
`4.3: the antitrust safety zone` MEANS
    BRANCH
      IF `1.0: whether the guidelines cover licensing of` (a's `the form of the intellectual property licensed`) EQUALS `not covered: these guidelines do not cover the antitrust treatment of trademarks`
        THEN NOTHING
      IF NOT a's `the restraint is in a licensing arrangement`
        THEN JUST (`the safety zone does not apply` `the restraint is not in a licensing arrangement`)
      IF NOT a's `the restraint is related to the use of the licensed intellectual property`
        THEN JUST (`the safety zone does not apply` `the restraint is unrelated to the use of the licensed intellectual property`)
      IF    merger EQUALS `the agencies will apply a merger analysis: an outright sale of all rights to the intellectual property`
         OR merger EQUALS `the agencies will apply a merger analysis: an exclusive license`
        THEN JUST (`the safety zone does not apply` `the agencies apply a merger analysis to the transfer`)
      IF merger EQUALS `the agencies may also apply a merger analysis: a license that in substance transfers the rights`
        THEN NOTHING
      IF `4.3: the restraint is facially anticompetitive` (a's `the restraint`)
        THEN JUST (`outside the safety zone: the agencies will analyze the arrangement on the considerations of parts 3 to 5, and it is not anticompetitive merely for being outside` `the restraint is facially anticompetitive`)
      IF null considered
        THEN NOTHING
      IF NOT null failing
        THEN JUST (`outside the safety zone: the agencies will analyze the arrangement on the considerations of parts 3 to 5, and it is not anticompetitive merely for being outside` (`a relevant market significantly affected by the restraint does not meet its criterion` (map (GIVEN m YIELD m's `the name of the market`) failing)))
      IF any (GIVEN m YIELD `4.3: the market meets its criterion` m EQUALS NOTHING) considered
        THEN NOTHING
      OTHERWISE JUST `inside the safety zone: absent extraordinary circumstances, the agencies will not challenge the restraint`
  WHERE
    merger MEANS `5.7: merger analysis of the transfer` (a's `the transfer`)
    considered MEANS `4.3: the markets by reference to which the safety zone is determined` a
    failing MEANS filter (GIVEN m YIELD `4.3: the market meets its criterion` m EQUALS JUST FALSE) considered
